# {{lb|en|UK}} Someone who has [[coeliac disease]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1961|author=Association of National European and Mediterranean Societies of Gastroenterology|title=Proceedings VIth meeting of the "Association des Sociétés Nationales Européenes et Méditerranéennes de Gastro-Entérologie"|page=624|url=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=i8QwAAAAIAAJ&q=%22coeliacs%22+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&dq=%22coeliacs%22+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=sywtT7OEJqq5iAeHkLHODg&redir_esc=y|passage=In all 5 untreated '''coeliacs''' as well as the 3 partially treated '''coeliacs''' who were in relapse at the time of biopsy, villi were entirely absent.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1986|author=David R. Triger|title=Clinical Immunology of the Liver and Gastrointestinal Tract|page=67|url=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=GTZsAAAAMAAJ&q=%22coeliacs%22+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&dq=%22coeliacs%22+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=4SktT6X5MouhiQfC-fDQDg&redir_esc=y|passage=Hyposplenism in '''coeliacs''' does not appear to lead to these diseases.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1999|author=Giuseppe Gobbi|title=Epilepsy and Other Neurological Disorders in Coeliac Disease|page=212|url=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=T3q_sQ9f110C&pg=PA212&dq=%22coeliacs%22+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=RygtT771EIWtiAfkg8jYDg&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22coeliacs%22%20-intitle%3A%22%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false|passage=Instead, anecdotal observations came to dominate the literature, describing adult '''coeliacs''' as mentally peculiar, excessively nervous and unstable, depressive, or even schizophrenic (Paulley, 1959; Dohan, 1966).}}